    "case_file": "{\n  \"plugin\": \"regex-infer\",\n  \"task\": \"infer-pattern\",\n  \"cases\": [\n    {\n      \"prompt\": \"Task: infer-pattern; case: widget-code.\\n\\nInfer the hidden string rule from the labelled visible examples in input.json. Return a Python regular expression, evaluated with re.fullmatch, which describes the entire string. Anchors are optional. Do not simply list the accepted examples: grading uses a separate held-out set. You may test a candidate on the visible examples. The pattern must be nonblank, have no surrounding whitespace, and contain at most 120 characters. The verifier also rejects a group containing a quantifier when that group is itself quantified with *, +, or a counted repetition. The hidden rule and held-out examples are not supplied.\\n\\nRead input.json using any available tools. Work efficiently; no particular tool or full-data display is required. Do not modify input.json or prompt.txt. Write only the final answer object to answer.json, then stop. Use these exact fields and types; do not add fields.\\n\\nAnswer JSON Schema:\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"case\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"enum\\\":[\\\"widget-code\\\"]},\\\"pattern\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"pattern\\\"],\\\"additionalProperties\\\":false}\",\n      \"arguments\": {\n        \"case\": \"widget-code\"\n      },\n      \"fixtures\": \"public\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"refuse\": []\n}",
